            {
              "id": 2,
              "request_id": 1,
              "created_at": 1793596157,
              "web_search_used": false,
              "addressed_to": "",
              "output_tokens": 532,
              "text": "Writer has access to the two folders through different **Files** scopes:\n\n| Folder | Where it is referenced | Who gets access |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Docs OpenAI** | **Forums \u2192 Lab \u2192 Files** | Every character answering in Lab, including Writer |\n| **Docs Gemini** | **Characters \u2192 Writer \u2192 Character settings \u2192 Files** | Writer, in any forum it joins |\n\nWriter\u2019s saved provider is **openai-direct**, using OpenAI Responses in network mode. With that provider:\n\n- **Docs OpenAI** can use OpenAI\u2019s native **File Search** if its ready store was uploaded to OpenAI with the **same saved key ID** as Writer\u2019s provider. OpenAI supports at most two native stores.\n- **Docs Gemini**, if uploaded to Google, is searched through CHA\u2019s **`search_attached_files`** tool using the upload\u2019s saved key. Writer does **not** need to use a Gemini model to search it; the answering model must support function calls.\n\nThe folder names alone do not establish the upload service or key. I verified the saved references and Writer\u2019s provider, but these configuration reads do not establish either store\u2019s readiness or upload-key match.\n\nIn a **Lab** conversation, address Writer explicitly, for example:\n\n> @Writer Search Docs OpenAI and Docs Gemini for how file search works. Compare the approaches and identify the supporting documents.\n\n**Relevant limits:** both folders need ready stores and available upload keys. A Gemini 2.5 model using native File Search cannot also use `search_attached_files`; CHA omits that tool and its folders in that case. Welcome does not search folder references.\n\nIf the chat toolbar has a **Model** or **Effort** override for Writer, it applies only to that session. Set both to **Default** to use Writer\u2019s configured provider and effort. `/detach <Ref ID>` removes only a folder attached directly in chat\u2014it does not remove either of these saved **Files** references.",
